* =====================================================================================================
* ti/tps22917 view "lsw" (breadboard.dev, Apache-2.0): TPS22917 load switch, DATASHEET-FITTED behavioural
* model, valid at the fast and pi rungs.  Written for Phase 1 plan M5b (ADR-006 D9 rule 4) and RESTATED in
* Phase 2 P1 to ADR-009 D2's rules (approver decision D-TPS): no branch-current unknown (no V-type B
* source), and no internal node held only by a microsiemens path.  It contains no text of TI's SLVMCE8
* PSpice model and no element of the dial-me-spinner suite's vendor-derived view; every number below is a
* datasheet value or a stated assumption.
*
* Datasheet: TI SLVSDW8B (TPS22917, September 2017, revised December 2021), opened for the P1 restatement:
*   Table 7.3  ON: VIH >= 1.0 V, VIL <= 0.35 V (guaranteed window only; no typical trip point).
*   Table 7.5  RON typ at IOUT 200 mA, 25 C: 220 / 170 / 120 / 90 / 80 mOhm at VIN 1.0 / 1.2 / 1.8 / 3.6 / 5 V;
*              QOD 150 Ohm (disabled); RPD 750 kOhm (VON <= VIL); IQ,VIN 0.5 uA typ (enabled);
*              ISD,VIN 10 nA typ (disabled, VOUT = GND).
*   Table 7.6  (CL 1 uF, RL 10 Ohm, 25 C) tON per pF of CT: 3 / 3.4 / 3.6 / 3.8 / 4 us/pF at VIN 1.0 / 1.2 / 1.8 /
*              3.6 / 5 V; tR per pF: 0.6 / 0.95 / 1.2 / 1.6 / 1.8 us/pF; SRON 1100 / 1000 / 1100 / 1900 / 2300
*              (mV/us) pF; tON with CT open 120 us at 3.6 V; tOFF 10 us.  Section 9.3.2: turn-on time =
*              CT x tON, from enable to VOUT at 90 % of VIN.
*
* Structure (every current a B CURRENT source of node voltages, or a plain R or C; every internal signal an
* I-type B source into a 1 Ohm conductance, ADR-009 D2 rule 1):
*   enable   ON comparator with hysteresis (rising 0.68 V, falling 0.63 V: inside Table 7.3's window, an
*            ASSUMED trip point), into 1 Ohm; then a 2 us RC (the enable delay), its resistor an I-type
*            source of the two nodes (0.5 mS).
*   VINF     VIN low-passed with 1 ms (1 S into 1 mF), for the slew constants only, so a VIN sag of the
*            switch's own making cannot steer them.  (Before P1 this was 1 uS into 1 nF: a node held by
*            1 uS, which gave ngspice a singular matrix at an operating point, ADR-009 Amendment 1 item 6.)
*   CT       while enabled the CT pin sinks I = VINF / tONk, so the CT-to-VIN capacitance (external CT plus
*            C_int) swings x = (VIN - V(CT)) / VINF from 0 to 1 in exactly tON = tONk * (CT + C_int); the
*            sink fades out at x = 1.10..1.12 (the CT pin then sits about 0.1 VIN below ground; the real pin
*            voltage is not specified).  While disabled CT is reset to VIN through 10 kOhm.
*   target   Vt = VINF * (0.9 - 0.8 * (1 - x) * tONk / tRk): a linear ramp that crosses 10 % of VIN at
*            tON - tR and 90 % at tON (Table 7.6's tON and tRk below; its slope is 0.8 VIN / tR, which a
*            linear ramp cannot match together with Table 7.6's SRON).  A 50 mV softplus rounds its start.
*   pass     I(VIN -> VOUT) = en * max(0, min(GF * (Vt - VOUT), (VIN - VOUT) / RON)): VOUT follows the
*            ramp (GF = 20 S) and the switch is RON once the ramp passes VIN.  Forward only: VOUT above
*            VIN draws no reverse current (reverse current blocking).
*   QOD      150 Ohm from QOD to GND while disabled (Table 7.5).  1 GOhm from QOD to VOUT keeps the pin
*            defined when it is left floating (the datasheet's way to disable QOD).
*   ON pin   750 kOhm pull-down while the comparator reads low (Table 7.5 RPD).
*   supply   IQ 0.5 uA while enabled; ISD 5 nA while disabled (an ASSUMED value below Table 7.5's 10 nA
*            typ, as before P1).
*
* tONk, tRk (us/pF) are interpolated in VIN between the Table 7.6 columns and scaled by 1000/(1000 + 32) so
* that CT = 1000 pF gives the table values with C_int = 32 pF included; C_int = 32 pF gives the CT-open tON
* (118 us at 3.6 V against 120 us typ).  At 3.6 and 5 V tRk is Table 7.6's tR row; at 1, 1.2 and 1.8 V it
* is 0.8 VIN / SRON (0.727 / 0.96 / 1.309 us/pF), as in Phase 1, not the tR row (0.6 / 0.95 / 1.2): a
* linear ramp cannot meet both there, and the tR row moved E1's cold VLED ramp (VSYS 3.0 V) by about
* 40 us, beyond its recorded 1 mV / 1 sample snapshot (approver decision D-TPS: E1's fast results stay
* within their recorded tolerances; ADR-009 Amendment 4).  RON is interpolated in VIN between the
* Table 7.5 typ columns.
*
* The pin nodes CT and QOD keep their 1 GOhm keepers (the open-pin cases of the datasheet: a board
* connects them, and the CT sink's own slope holds CT where it fades out); every internal node has at
* least 0.5 mS to GNDP or to its driving node in every state (ADR-009 D2 rule 2), and every division by
* an internal node is guarded by a max() that is inactive at any solution (tONk >= 2.9, tRk >= 0.58,
* RON >= 0.08), so a Newton iterate at 0 V never divides by zero.  Every internal node also has a plain
* resistor (1 Ohm to GNDP for the signals; 1 GOhm keepers from lsf_en to lsf_ont and from lsf_vinf to
* VIN, beside the B sources that drive them, so they change no DC value): measured in P1, ngspice's
* source stepping reports a node whose only DC path is a B source as singular (ADR-009 Amendment 4).
*
* Parameters (the same as the vendor-derived view, so the two are interchangeable in a project):
*   ron_add  extra pass resistance (Ohm), e.g. Table 7.5's RON max rows.
*   isd_out  VIN -> VOUT leakage (A) while disabled (Table 7.5 ISD max as a worst case).
*
* NOT modelled: temperature; RON's dependence on IOUT; QOD's dependence on VIN (150 Ohm flat); the
*   current-limited ramp when the load exceeds GF * error; reverse current blocking thresholds and timing
*   (reverse current is simply never conducted); thermal shutdown; ESD structures; tolerance and
*   part-to-part spread.
* Ports: CT GNDP ON QOD VIN VOUT (the package's pin names CT GND ON QOD VIN VOUT; GND is renamed GNDP, the
*   gnd rule of spec/package.md section 5).
* =====================================================================================================
.subckt TI_TPS22917_LSW_FIT CT GNDP ON QOD VIN VOUT params: ron_add=0 isd_out=0
* ---- enable: comparator with hysteresis into 1 Ohm, then a 2 us RC
B_ONT    GNDP lsf_ont I = 0.5 + 0.5*tanh((V(ON,GNDP) - 0.68 + 0.05*V(lsf_en,GNDP))/0.005)
R_ONT    lsf_ont GNDP 1
B_EN     GNDP lsf_en I = (V(lsf_ont,GNDP) - V(lsf_en,GNDP))/2k
C_EN     lsf_en GNDP 1n
R_ENL    lsf_en lsf_ont 1G
B_RPD    ON GNDP I = V(ON,GNDP)/750k * (1 - V(lsf_en,GNDP))
* ---- VIN low-passed (1 ms: 1 S into 1 mF), for the slew constants only
B_VF     GNDP lsf_vinf I = V(VIN,GNDP) - V(lsf_vinf,GNDP)
C_VF     lsf_vinf GNDP 1m
R_VFL    lsf_vinf VIN 1G
* ---- tONk, tRk (us/pF) at VINF; scaled by 1000/1032 for C_int (header)
B_TONK   GNDP lsf_tonk I = 0.968992 * pwl(V(lsf_vinf,GNDP), 0,3.0, 1,3.0, 1.2,3.4, 1.8,3.6, 3.6,3.8, 5,4.0, 5.5,4.0)
R_TONK   lsf_tonk GNDP 1
B_TRK    GNDP lsf_trk I = 0.968992 * pwl(V(lsf_vinf,GNDP), 0,0.727273, 1,0.727273, 1.2,0.96, 1.8,1.309091, 3.6,1.6, 5,1.8, 5.5,1.8)
R_TRK    lsf_trk GNDP 1
* ---- CT: internal capacitance, sink while enabled, reset to VIN while disabled
C_INT    CT VIN 32p
R_CTL    CT VIN 1G
B_CT     CT GNDP I = V(lsf_en,GNDP) * max(V(lsf_vinf,GNDP),0)/(1e6*max(V(lsf_tonk,GNDP),0.1)) * min(1, max(0, (1.12 - V(VIN,CT)/max(V(lsf_vinf,GNDP),0.5))/0.02))
B_CTR    VIN CT I = (1 - V(lsf_en,GNDP)) * V(VIN,CT)/10k
* ---- VOUT target: linear ramp through 10 % at tON - tR and 90 % at tON, softplus start
B_VT     GNDP lsf_vt I = max(V(lsf_vinf,GNDP),0) * (0.9 - 0.8*(1 - V(VIN,CT)/max(V(lsf_vinf,GNDP),0.5)) * V(lsf_tonk,GNDP)/max(V(lsf_trk,GNDP),0.1))
R_VT     lsf_vt GNDP 1
B_VTS    GNDP lsf_vts I = V(lsf_vt,GNDP) > 1 ? V(lsf_vt,GNDP) : 0.05*ln(1 + exp(min(V(lsf_vt,GNDP)/0.05, 40)))
R_VTS    lsf_vts GNDP 1
* ---- RON (Table 7.5 typ, interpolated in VIN) + ron_add
B_RON    GNDP lsf_ron I = pwl(V(VIN,GNDP), 0,0.22, 1,0.22, 1.2,0.17, 1.8,0.12, 3.6,0.09, 5,0.08, 5.5,0.08) + {ron_add}
R_RON    lsf_ron GNDP 1
* ---- pass element: forward-only follower of the target, limited by RON
B_PASS   VIN VOUT I = V(lsf_en,GNDP) * max(0, min(20*(V(lsf_vts,GNDP) - V(VOUT,GNDP)), V(VIN,VOUT)/max(V(lsf_ron,GNDP),0.01)))
* ---- quick output discharge while disabled
B_QOD    QOD GNDP I = V(QOD,GNDP)/150 * (1 - V(lsf_en,GNDP))
R_QODL   QOD VOUT 1G
* ---- supply current, and the optional disabled-state leakage to VOUT
B_IQ     VIN GNDP I = (0.5u*V(lsf_en,GNDP) + 5n*(1 - V(lsf_en,GNDP))) * min(1, max(0, V(VIN,GNDP)))
B_ISD    VIN VOUT I = {isd_out} * (1 - V(lsf_en,GNDP))
.ends TI_TPS22917_LSW_FIT
